  "project_description": "The Commerce Fee module provides a UI for defining fees (surcharges) that Drupal Commerce adds to order totals. It mirrors the architecture of Commerce Promotion: each fee is a content entity that pairs a fee-offer plugin (fixed amount or percentage, at order or order-item level) with a set of commerce conditions, order types, stores, and a start/end date window. An order processor evaluates available fees during the order refresh and records each one as a positive 'fee' adjustment on the order or its order items, so fees flow through Commerce's normal pricing, tax, and refund machinery.",
